From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mikael Hug <mikaelhug@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:11:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: brcmfmac: hold the wiphy lock when stopping the primary
 interface

brcmf_del_if() stops the primary interface by calling brcmf_netdev_stop()
directly, under RTNL only. That reaches brcmf_abort_scanning(), which
reads cfg->scan_request and completes it with cfg80211_scan_done().
cfg80211 calls the scan operation with the wiphy mutex held, not RTNL,
so nothing serialises the two. When the scan operation fails, it clears
cfg->scan_request and returns the error, and nl80211_trigger_scan()
frees the request. The detach path can read the pointer before it is
cleared and complete a request that is already freed.

On a Mac mini M2 (BCM4388) this happened when brcmfmac was unloaded
while the firmware had stopped answering. The scan's dcmd timed out
after 2 s while rmmod ran:

  brcmf_msgbuf_query_dcmd: Timeout on response for query command
  brcmf_run_escan: error (-5)
  brcmf_cfg80211_scan: scan error (-5)
  WARNING: net/wireless/scan.c:1229 at cfg80211_scan_done+0x78/0x1f0 [cfg80211]
  Unable to handle kernel paging request at virtual address 00000000059ffff0
  pc : _raw_spin_lock_irqsave+0x34/0x8c
  lr : wiphy_work_queue+0x30/0x184 [cfg80211]
   brcmf_notify_escan_complete+0x130/0x29c [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_abort_scanning+0x4c/0xe4 [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_cfg80211_down+0x60/0x100 [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_remove_interface+0x230/0x274 [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_detach+0x90/0x198 [brcmfmac]
   brcmf_pcie_remove+0xa0/0x180 [brcmfmac]

The oops left RTNL held, so every later netlink user hung.

On a normal ifdown this cannot happen. The NETDEV_GOING_DOWN notifier
takes the wiphy mutex before ndo_stop runs, so a scan operation in
progress has returned by then. Take the wiphy mutex inside RTNL around
the direct call as well, the same way brcmf_detach() already removes
the P2P device interface since commit 08a3f02fea63 ("wifi: brcmfmac:
fix P2P device removal race in brcmf_detach()").

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01UqitcmCNS6G33aQUShi39x
---
 drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
index 13cb6cb..f6b0c1b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/broadcom/brcm80211/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -936,7 +936,9 @@ static void brcmf_del_if(struct brcmf_pub *drvr, s32 bsscfgidx,
 		if (bsscfgidx == 0) {
 			if (ifp->ndev->netdev_ops == &brcmf_netdev_ops_pri) {
 				rtnl_lock();
+				wiphy_lock(drvr->wiphy);
 				brcmf_netdev_stop(ifp->ndev);
+				wiphy_unlock(drvr->wiphy);
 				rtnl_unlock();
 			}
 		} else {
